<p>Honestly, the amount of CSS knowledge you need to make a theme is extremely minimal. I barely knew anything beyond making a div before I edited the MC&amp;D theme and have since gone on to create/revise multiple themes. The Wilson's theme is hopefully commented well enough that you should just be able to read it with a basic understanding of CSS terms are and figure out what things do.</p>
<p>While I think there is probably some kind of problem with themes, the solution to that problem is in no way being elitist gatekeepers and restricting basic information that is already publically accessible and easy to find. Do you also think CSS themes should be bloated and uncommented messes? Or we should actively hide the code of themes on site, to prevent them from being modified?</p>

