														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4189125">
									

<p>The problem with your argument is that this is not an educational resource, it is a tool for <em>creating</em> CSS themes, which lowers the amount of knowledge you need from &quot;minimal&quot; to &quot;zero&quot;. I don't think it's particularly elitist to say that the barrier for entry to creating a CSS theme should be demonstrating, by seeking out and using aforementioned publicly accessible information, the competence and initiative necessary to maintain said theme in the long-term. It's no different than requiring site applicants to read the guides before joining the site &#8212; basic quality control is not gatekeeping.</p>

