			<div class="content" id="post-content-4189349">
									

<p>To cite an age old cliche &#8212; I think we'll just have to politely agree to disagree. Restricting access to a tool because you think it will lead to a glut of fugly art is, to me, the very antithesis of collaborative artistic expression.</p>
<p>If this puts an undue burden on staff (because they have to run around and take down five billion themes that break on mobile), that's one thing. I can understand how <em>that's</em> an issue. But permitting more people to express themselves with greater ease? That's, in my mind, entirely a good thing.</p>

