			<div class="content" id="post-content-4190684">
									

<p>Given that we’ve got an official CSS policy that requires things like this not break functionality and be accessible for everyone, having tools to make simple ones on-site is at least something we’re nominally ready for policy-wise. I’m not happy our tech team’s will was unintentionally subverted but I hope this doesn’t lead to any knee-jerk reactions against CSS themes(not singling out tech team, whom I can’t recall being guilty of this anytime recently, I’ve just been on staff long enough to know how these things shake out a lot of the time both in terms of staff and users being reactionary) and acting in the heat of the moment.</p>

							</div>

